/E (The Shabbat between Rosh Hashanah and Yom Kippur is called Shabbat Shuvah, "Shabbat of Return." The name derives from the Haftarah for this Shabbat, which opens with the words \(Hosea 14:2\), "Return O Israel unto the L-rd your G-d..." Occurring in the Ten Days of Repentance, it is a most auspicious time to rectify the failings and missed opportunities of the past and positively influence the coming year.)
