<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 165 0 R
/E (In 1977, while leading hakafot with thousands of chassidim in the main Chabad-Lubavitch synagogue in Brooklyn, the Rebbe suffered a massive heart attack but remained calm and continued the hakafot until they concluded. The next day, he asked that Simchat Torah be celebrated with its usual joy, and it was. After the holiday, he addressed anxious chassidim from his office, which had been converted into a cardiac unit. He remained under medical supervision for several weeks before returning home five weeks later, on 1 Kislev, a day now marked by chassidim as a day of celebration and thanksgiving.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [38]
>>
